{{Codex|The Supra is a heavy laser gun with a short wind up time.}}

The '''Supra''' is a {{Faction|Corpus}} tri-barrel laser minigun unlockable through Energy Lab [[Research]] in the [[Dojo]]. It is used by [[Corpus Tech]]s and sometimes by [[Warden|Corpus Wardens]] throughout Corpus-controlled regions, and is effectively the Corpus standard machine gun.

==Characteristics==
*This weapon deals primarily {{D|Puncture}} damage.
*Requires a spool-up of '''5''' shots before optimal fire rate is achieved.
**Fire rate starts at '''10%''' of the listed value, and increases by '''22.5%''' per shot.
*Can equip the Supra-exclusive {{M|Directed Convergence}} and {{M|Entropy Burst}} mods.

{{Advantages|name=Supra|class=Rifle|trigger=Auto-Spool|}}

{{Disadvantages|name=Supra|class=Rifle|trigger=Auto-Spool|
* Projectiles have travel time, making long range shots more difficult.
* Spool-up creates a warm-up period of weakness for fire rate, making short engagements undesirable.
}}

{{WeaponComparison|Supra Vandal}}

==Acquisition==
The Supra's blueprint can be [[research]]ed from the [[Research/Energy Lab|Energy Lab]] in the [[dojo]].

{{BuildAutomatic|type=Weapon}}
This weapon can be sold for {{cc|7,500}}.

==Notes==
*Cancelling the reload animation on its third-quarter period counts as a reload, much like the {{Weapon|Soma}}.

==Tips==
*Supra has a decent fire rate like the Gorgon, but it is less accurate at longer distances. Firing in short bursts may help with accuracy.
*Alternatively, use the mods {{M|Stabilizer}} or {{M|Vile Precision}} to reduce the high recoil, and make it more comfortable to fire overall.
*To counter the weapon's quick ammo consumption, it would be ideal to bring [[Squad Ammo Restore]]s, {{M|Rifle Ammo Mutation}}, [[Carrier]] with {{M|Ammo Case}}, {{M|Vigilante Supplies}} and/or the {{M|Rifle Scavenger}} [[aura]].
*{{M|Shred}} or {{M|Metal Auger}} can help hit more enemies, somewhat balancing the high ammo consumption.

==Trivia==
*''[[wiktionary:supra#Latin|Supra]]'' is Latin for "above".
*The Supra's magazine is the large boxy object on the top of the gun, and presumably doubles as a sight due to the notch.
*The Supra's energy goes dark when the magazine has been taken out during reloading, and will light up again after the magazine has been replaced.
**The magazine might be a battery or fuel as opposed to ammunition, due to this
*The Supra is the first weapon to receive two augment mods; {{M|Entropy Burst}} from the [[Cephalon Suda]] Syndicate and {{M|Directed Convergence}} from the [[Conclave]] Syndicate.
*Although the Supra is labeled as a "laser gun" in its description. It is actually a plasma weapon.

